      "observed": "Net /NET0069 contains only the anodes of LEDs D21, D37, and D43; it has no supply, driver, or other component node. D19's anode, by contrast, is connected to +3V3.",
      "expected": "Discrete LED anodes should be connected to a supply rail (e.g. +3V3) or an appropriate driven node so the LEDs can light. The netlist shows a floating common-anode net, which is not a normal functional connection.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"17\") (name \"/NET0069\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"D21\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"D37\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"D43\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+3V3\") ... (node (ref \"D19\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\"))"}
      ],
      "impact": "D21, D37, and D43 cannot conduct and will remain dark; any status or Ethernet/activity indication they provide will not work.",
      "confidence": 0.75
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U19", "U20"],
      "pins": ["U19.4", "U19.5", "U20.4", "U20.5"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "The isolated CAN transceivers U19 and U20 have both GND1 and GND2 pins connected to the same system GND net. Their bus-side supplies are also not isolated from the logic-side ground.",
      "expected": "For an isolated CAN bus implementation, the transceiver's GND1 and GND2 should be separate grounds (or the design should use a non-isolated transceiver if isolation is not intended). The specification describes two isolated CAN buses.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (`CAN0`, `CAN1`), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller ... through an isolated CAN transceiver"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"53\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"U19\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\") (pintype \"power_in\")) (node (ref \"U19\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") (pintype \"power_in\")) (node (ref \"U20\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\") (pintype \"power_in\")) (node (ref \"U20\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"}
      ],
      "impact": "The galvanic isolation of the CAN interfaces is defeated; the buses share the same ground as the logic side, removing the intended isolation benefit and allowing ground loops/common-mode coupling.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist supports at least one functional deviation: a common LED-anode net is floating with no supply, leaving D21/D37/D43 dark. A second likely deviation is that the isolated CAN transceiver grounds are tied together, contradicting the specified isolated CAN architecture."
}

